  "description": "K-way external merge sort for .NET 8. Sort datasets larger than available memory using binary min-heap merge. v1.0.4 parallelizes the merge phase (per-pass batches merge concurrently, ~1.54x end-to-end vs the old serial-merge ~1.20x ceiling) and hardens the library: option validation, leak-safe streams, Int64 counts for billion-record sorts, and real BytesRead/BytesWritten metrics. Builds on pipelined parallel chunk creation, Knuth's Replacement Selection (~2x larger runs), and a ReplaceMin merge fast path. Generic IExternalSorter<T> — plug in any record type, comparer, and serializer.",
